  "body": "Part of #1503 (its Expected item 2, split out so the safety fix for item 1 can land on its own).\n\nThe maintainer (2026-11-13, on #1503): \"This should be integrated as a method for 'Adaptive' clearing tho, not a slot that doesnt confine itself within the selection.. Its an adaptive strategy\".\n\nWhat is wanted: trochoidal motion offered as a strategy of 2D Adaptive clearing - a method choice on the Adaptive operation, with a default, working inside the selected region and its boundary settings - not only as a free-standing slot placed by two typed points. What happens to the stand-alone Trochoidal slot operation (kept as a confined slot, or folded into Adaptive with old projects migrated) is recorded in the PR's decision file.\n\nRelated: #220 (trochoidal toolpaths, Adaptive mode + standalone op), #5 (trochoidal Adaptive in slot-width channels and thin bands), #6 (3D Adaptive trochoidal). Check those for overlap before starting.\n\nDone means: 2D Adaptive has a trochoidal method that stays inside its region (golden CL, engagement within the limit); undo, MCP parameter and the structural UI test cover the new choice.\n",
